From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: s5k3l6: Leave the phase detection pixels
 uncorrected at full size

The S5K3L6 has 32 half-shielded phase detection pixels in each 64x64
block, on blue sites. The Windows settings have the sensor correct them
in every mode (bit 2 of register 0x3403, written as part of 0x3402), so
the frame carries no phase information.

Clear that bit in the 4160x3120 mode, as the vendors' drivers do in
their phase detection modes, so that the camera stack can measure the
phase from the frame; the ISP then corrects these pixels in the image.
The other modes keep the correction: as in the vendors' drivers, phase
detection uses the full size mode only.

On an S5K3L6 unit, clearing the bit changes exactly these 32 pixels per
block of a flat field (by 16 to 18 percent), and no other. Over a lens
sweep on a textured target, the phase measured from these pixels changes
linearly with the lens position and crosses zero near the contrast peak.
On a photo of a plain wall, the pixels corrected by the ISP stand out by
at most about 0.4 percent of the level, about as much as on a photo of
white paper taken with the sensor's own correction.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k3l6.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3l6.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3l6.c
index 377c737f36..4424f48be0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3l6.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3l6.c
@@ -214,9 +214,11 @@ static const struct cci_reg_sequence s5k3l6_init_regs_b[] = {
 };
 
 /*
- * In every mode, the 16-bit write to 0x3402 sets 0x3403 to 0x46, whose bit 2
- * has the sensor correct its phase detection pixels (32 per 64x64 block, on
- * blue sites), as the Windows settings do.
+ * The 16-bit write to 0x3402 sets 0x3403, whose bit 2 has the sensor correct
+ * its phase detection pixels (32 per 64x64 block, on blue sites). The Windows
+ * settings set it in every mode. The 4160x3120 mode clears it, for phase
+ * detection from the frame, and the ISP corrects these pixels in the image;
+ * the other modes keep it.
  */
 static const struct cci_reg_sequence s5k3l6_4160x3120_regs[] = {
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x0344), 0x0020 },
@@ -262,7 +264,7 @@ static const struct cci_reg_sequence s5k3l6_4160x3120_regs[] = {
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x314a), 0x5f00 },
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x3300), 0x0000 },
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x3400), 0x0000 },
-	{ CCI_REG16(0x3402), 0x4e46 },
+	{ CCI_REG16(0x3402), 0x4e42 },	/* 0x3403 bit 2 clear, see above */
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x32b2), 0x0006 },
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x32b4), 0x0006 },
 	{ CCI_REG16(0x32b6), 0x0006 },
